{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332765-physical-beings-in-the-shadowlands","id":332765,"title":"Physical beings in the Shadowlands","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-06T22:42:50-08:00","id":332765,"title":"Physical beings in the Shadowlands","content":"So, as I've always understood it - the Skinland structures and inhabitants are completely visible (if warped) in the Shadowlands, and exert physical force. Wraiths can't exert physical force back without Arcanoi, and spend corpus to step through said structures or beings if they can't step around them.<br /> <br /> So how does it actually work for others who PHYSICALLY travel to the &quot;Dark Umbra&quot;, be they Mages, Werewolves, Vampires, whatever? How do they handle the closed doors in the Shadowlands that Wraiths spend corpus to step through?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T23:14:27-08:00","id":332781,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">*That* is an excellent question!<br /> <br /> RAW Answer: I\u2019m not sure there is one. I'm hoping this will be one of those things that Wr20 addresses.<br /> <br /> Using the setting as is (Second Edition), I\u2019d be inclined to rule that they\u2019re S.O.L. The Underworld is for the Dead, not the living (nor the undead).<br /> <br /> Of course, if Mr. D. weighted in, he could \u2013 maybe \u2013 give us a sneak peak at the Shadowland\u2019s Revised necrophysics &lt;wink wink nudge nudge&gt;.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As always, my two Oboli. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T00:20:49-08:00","id":332847,"title":"","content":"Already thinking about what happens to mortals if they crossover to the Shadowlands, MANUALLY!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T02:10:32-08:00","id":332871,"title":"","content":"Well, in Mage, in the Book of Worlds, they detail the spheres and methods to travel to the various parts of the Umbra. The only method presented for the shadowlands is a rote called the Agama Sojourn (Entropy 4 Life 2 Spirit 3) which basically makes your character temporarily dead and sends you to the shadowlands. While there you have a corpus, just like a wraith, though you can still use magic. (Using Entropy magic in the shadowlands tends to open nihils and summon spectres, so beware) and traversing the other layers of the underworld requires a guide.<br /> <br /> The BOW doesn't provide any other methods of travel, and deals with it exclusively from the Euthanatos paradigm, and Entropy 4/Life 2/Spirit 3 as being the required spheres to make the trip. The Infinite Tapestry barely touches on the Low Umbra because the Wraith line at that point had ended, and there was more nothing to see.<br /> <br /> Xerxes Jones was able to travel to the shadowlands in some kind of voidship. Though if he piloted it as a psuedowraith, or had a real, physical body, I don't know. Maybe his voidship was specially designed to protect him from the dangers of the labyrinth (probably) and maybe he had such an excellent command of Entropy, Life, and Spirit that he bypassed the need for a corpus body... Or maybe the Euthanatos made it harder than it had to be and the writers of BOW didn't bother concerning themselves with any other method or paradigm of getting there. I think it's up to the individual ST.<br /> <br /> I know Xerxes is described in Mediums: Speakers with the Dead, but since I don't have that book I don't know if it details his methods of traveling to the Low Umbra.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T03:28:32-08:00","id":332883,"title":"","content":"Void Engineers (according to their Revised Tradition book) use the same Spheres, with the note that it's Life 4 (instead of 2) to physically enter &quot;Entropic Space&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T08:49:30-08:00","id":333011,"title":"","content":"In Mage:<br /> Maybe they would have to create some standing effect that would be allow them to reach back across the Shroud to affect the material world. So, not easy. And probably vulgar (after repetition). if very ghost-appropriate. (&quot;Did you just see that door open by itself?&quot; &quot;It was the wind&quot; &quot;Then how about the fact the OTHER door in the room just did the same thing in about the time it would take someone to cross the room?&quot;). <br /> <br /> Or make a buddy with a Wraith with Outrage to have him blow down the doors for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T13:32:53-08:00","id":333341,"title":"","content":"Necromancy's Ash Path, Level 4, allows a vampire to physically go to the Shadowlands. They act like an extra solid wraith: a vampire can spend a Health Level to became insubstantial for Stamina turns, like a Wraith. But they can only be hurt by things that cause aggravated damage in the Shadowlands, like Soulsteel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T21:00:20-08:00","id":333736,"title":"","content":"Looking oveer the available powers, I would say that insubstantialness is a property of being in the Dark Umbra/Shadowlands, and isn't exactly an inherent ability to wraiths. Now for 99.98% of what they do will be in the Underworld, so that's normal. A fully manifested Wraith doesn't go insubstantial though, since they are fully on the other side of the Shroud, if only for a little while.<br /> <br /> My thought is a mage would need to use some kind of effect to affect the physical world. I believe a vampire using Ex Nihilo could use the lower levels of the Ash path &quot;in reverse&quot; to affect the Skinlands if she had to. Werewolves I have much less info on, and other do not normally fully enter the Underworld proper. The Shadowlands as far as I can tell do not exist by Demon's timeline, so that's hard to say as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T21:32:42-08:00","id":333774,"title":"","content":"ok...for my experiences running games and bending rules....<br /> If anything Physical arrives into the Shadowlands, it slowly starts becoming part of it. What was once alive slowly dies and decays until he becomes a Wraith..or Worst.<br /> <br /> As for doors and such?<br /> Mages: Science!<br /> Werewolves: id magine they would use spirits or fetishes to move around and such<br /> Demons: If i recall, only Halaku's were able to enter the Domain of Death (Only Slayers) and ...lets put it in this perspective. &quot;No Door, Wall or Window can stop the Reaper..&quot;<br /> Hunters: they are stuck in our reality so, no problem there<br /> Changelings: i have this weird theory that if a changeling steps into Wraithland, he would die out of banality quiicker than you can say &quot;youre fucked.&quot;<br /> Vampires: If i dont bad remember, they were stuck in the EMOSPHERE/VAMPIRETOWN/BADYBADWORSTEVILMCMURDERTOWN/THE CULLENS FAMILY RETREAT you know what i mean..so basically.....WHY IN GODS NAME WOULD A VAMPIRE GET OUT OF THERE TO EXPLORE OBLIVION?! <br /> Human mere mortal stuck in that world?..ermm.....i have this mental image of Legend of Korra, of The Mists.. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6SsH1YFydiM\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6SsH1YFydiM</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T21:36:11-08:00","id":333776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332765-physical-beings-in-the-shadowlands?p=333774#post333774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters: they are stuck in our reality so, no problem there</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Hermits and anyone else who manages to get Solitude Edges can eventually look forward to getting Transcendence, which permits a kind of astral projection effect. That may not be the only way that it occurs, either, since the concept of alternate Edges only didn't get around to them because they were latecomers and painted as rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T21:44:40-08:00","id":333779,"title":"","content":"I believe technically how the Slayers worked is they opened up a door to the Maelstrom, flew through it however far they needed to, and exited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T00:19:09-08:00","id":333878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332765-physical-beings-in-the-shadowlands?p=333774#post333774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages: With Science Of Course!</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed.<br /> <br /> Not sure how the Legend of Kora comparison would work since both Aang and Kora have the same ability as Mages to move through the spirit world. I'm leaning to Flatliners, and The Frighteners. Was going to add Jacob's Ladder, but don't want to spoil the film.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T01:54:22-08:00","id":333987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332765-physical-beings-in-the-shadowlands?p=333774#post333774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings: i have this weird theory that if a changeling steps into Wraithland, he would die out of banality quiicker than you can say &quot;youre fucked.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings can traverse from the Dreaming to the Underworld (and, rarely, directly from Earth to the Underworld) through the use of a Black Path of Balor. The mechanics once they are in the Underworld were, to my recollection, never described. However, I'm sure it wasn't instant death by banality. Otherwise, what would be the point of having Black Paths of Balor? Sluagh and Keremet in particular are described as using them. However, beyond that, I can't recall anything that describes what happens when a Changeling physically enters the Shadowlands. I'd say that most rules that apply to a mortal apply to them, with Wyrd effects adjudicated on a case by case basis.<br /> <br /> I do remember that Sluagh can see wraiths by making a simple Perception+Kenning roll (I don't recall how difficult it is, though), and can hear them just by spending a point of Glamour. Pandemonium creates chimerical effects, and Keening is easier to use on a Changeling. I think it can also be combined with Ravaging to make it more effective, but I can't remember how. Phantasm has some weird effects when used on a Dreamer, but I forget what exactly. Nothing good for the Changeling trying to be the Dreamer's muse, if memory serves. On the other hand, using Phantasm to enter the Changeling's dreams is also possible, but usually not as safe for the Wraith making the attempt.<br /> <br /> For an even more unusual case, see the Keremet. They're listed among the Adhene (AKA the &quot;Denizens of the Dreaming&quot;), but they aren't really- they're enchanted mortals who were brought into the dreaming at the moment of their death. They can see, hear and communicate with Wraiths with no problem (no rolls or expenditures needed), and frequently pop in and out of the Underworld using the aforementioned Black Paths of Balor. One thing they do is ferry the souls that the Sidhe displace when they take a human host. But I still can't remember any specific rules for what they did once they were in the underworld. They didn't get much detail, I'm afraid. Like so much else in C:tD. :-(<br /> <br /> -Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T14:03:39-08:00","id":334530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NutiketAiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332765-physical-beings-in-the-shadowlands?p=333987#post333987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do remember that Sluagh can see wraiths by making a simple Perception+Kenning roll (I don't recall how difficult it is, though), and can hear them just by spending a point of Glamour. Pandemonium creates chimerical effects, and Keening is easier to use on a Changeling. I think it can also be combined with Ravaging to make it more effective, but I can't remember how. Phantasm has some weird effects when used on a Dreamer, but I forget what exactly. Nothing good for the Changeling trying to be the Dreamer's muse, if memory serves. On the other hand, using Phantasm to enter the Changeling's dreams is also possible, but usually not as safe for the Wraith making the attempt.<br /> -Jim</div> </div> </div> </div>The 2nd edition Wraith book says Perception+Alertness, difficulty 7, but that may be a Wraith shorthand.<br /> <br /> It also says that for a point of glamour they can converse with any wraiths in their immediate area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T14:20:48-08:00","id":334539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/332765-physical-beings-in-the-shadowlands?p=334530#post334530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The 2nd edition Wraith book says Perception+Alertness, difficulty 7, but that may be a Wraith shorthand.<br /> <br /> It also says that for a point of glamour they can converse with any wraiths in their immediate area.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I suspect they didn't want to introduce a new skill solely for the purposes of using Changeling NPCs in Wraith, so it's almost certainly shorthand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T16:06:37-08:00","id":334620,"title":"","content":"Wraiths have a very low Banality rating on average, so I don't think the Shadowlands would have that kind of effect on a Changeling. Given how chaotic and nightmarish the Underworld can be, I would wager that Bedlam would be a bigger risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}